    {
      "id": "b3",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "rv_cutaway",
      "spoken": "According to the lecture, the exhaust typically closes up to fifteen degrees after top dead centre, and the intake opens up to fifteen degrees before it. In that window exhaust gas can even flow back into the intake, especially at low speed and load. In the picture, that is the grey flow in the intake port.",
