    {
      "id": "b4",
      "function": "demonstration",
      "scene_type": "rv_board",
      "spoken": "Then more residual gas stays in the cylinder. The US Department of Energy calls fixed valve timing a compromise between low and high engine speeds. Variable timing saves three to four percent, according to the agency.",
