    {
      "id": "b5",
      "function": "insight",
      "scene_type": "rv_chart",
      "spoken": "So the overlap is only a few degrees of crank angle wide. But it helps decide how much residual gas stays in the cylinder and how well it fills with a fresh charge. That is why engineers care about those few degrees.",
